INT. NORTHBEAM SYNERGIES - OPEN OFFICE - MORNING

Rows of identical desks. A motivational banner reads "TOGETHER WE ALIGN." A broken printer wheezes in the corner.

BRENDA KOWALCZYK, 50s, regional VP in a power blazer, stands on a chair with a clicker. TREVOR NAKAMURA, 30s, middle manager, holds a coffee like a shield. PRIYA VENKATARAMAN, 30s, a senior analyst with a headset around her neck, scrolls through a spreadsheet. GUS TILLMAN, 20s, an intern in a too-big tie, takes notes.

BRENDA
Team! Huddle up!

Nobody huddles. Trevor drifts closer.

BRENDA (CONT'D)
Today we pivot. From synergy to hypersynergy.

TREVOR
(to himself)
Pivot where? We don't have a chair.

BRENDA
Trevor, I heard that.

TREVOR
I said "we don't have a chair." For the new hire.

BRENDA
We hire the person, not the chair.

PRIYA
(not looking up)
Brenda, our Q3 numbers are down forty percent.

BRENDA
Which is why we pivot.

PRIYA
It would be easier to fix the number.

BRENDA
We don't fix numbers, Priya. We reframe them.

GUS
(raising a hand)
Can I ask a question?

BRENDA
Gus. Welcome to the conversation.

GUS
What does hypersynergy mean?

BRENDA
It means synergy, but faster.

TREVOR
(to Gus, low)
It means layoffs.

BRENDA
I heard that too.

TREVOR
I know. I wanted you to.

Brenda climbs down from the chair, slowly, crosses to Trevor, and lowers her voice to a whisper that carries across the entire floor.

BRENDA
You're on a performance improvement plan.

TREVOR
For what?

BRENDA
For saying "layoffs" out loud.

PRIYA
(to herself, typing)
Seven words. A new record.

GUS
(to the room)
Does the plan come with a chair?

Priya snorts. Trevor stares at Brenda. Brenda stares back.

BRENDA
(to everyone)
Everyone back to your desks. We're going to have a very productive day.

Nobody moves. The printer coughs and dies.

TREVOR
I'm not on a plan.

BRENDA
You are now.

TREVOR
Then I quit.

PRIYA
Seconded.

GUS
(very small)
Does that include interns?

Brenda looks at the banner, then at the three of them, then at the dead printer. Her smile has not moved at all.

BRENDA
Everybody take fifteen. In fifteen minutes, we circle back to this.

She steps back up onto the chair.
